	(gr_text "Origin = device (2,84) on the Fusion model: kx = x-2, ky = 84-y. Locked parts = SS_revC3_placement.csv. Unlocked parts are parked right of the board: place them in the zones."
		(at 100 96 0)
		(layer "Cmts.User")
		(uuid "6bc74bfc-975d-4e77-9fea-cf1044b62aa9")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.8 0.8)
				(thickness 0.12)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "ROUTING GUIDE (base board C.5)  -  route in this order, run DRC after each step\nLayers: F.Cu signals + front parts | In1 = solid GND plane, never route | In2 = power rails | B.Cu signals + back parts\n0  Setup: open SignalScout_Base.kicad_pro (not the .kicad_pcb), press B to fill zones. J1 = Hirose FH35C-39S-0.3SHW, the panel connects through the flex jumper board.\n1  LoRa RF: U2 pin 21 (top-right corner of the E22) to J3 pin 1 along the top edge on B.Cu. 50 ohm CPWG (Calculator: 1.0 mm board, L4 over L2),\n   no vias, no bends sharper than 45 deg, GND via fence both sides every 1.5 mm. Nothing else may cross it.\n2  GNSS RF: ANT1 feed (right pad) -> C24 -> R24 -> C25 -> U3 pin 11, B.Cu, same CPWG rules, as short as possible. Stay out of the antenna keep-out.\n3  USB: J2 D+/D- -> U9 (front, through 2 vias) -> U1 pins 13/14. Diff pair tool (key 6), 90 ohm, same layer, length-matched, no stubs.\n4  Display QSPI: J1 LCD_SCK, D0-D3, CS -> U1. Route as a group, within 5 mm of each other, 0.15 mm, over In1. Keep away from L1 and U12.\n5  Power (back left strip): J2 VBUS -> U10 pin 13 on In2, 0.5 mm. U10 VSYS -> U12 -> L1 -> C7/C8 = one tight loop on B.Cu, 0.6-0.8 mm.\n   J8 (battery pads) -> U10 pins 2/3 0.8 mm. Nothing under L1. Power vias 0.8/0.4, at least 2 per layer change.\n6  Rails on In2: +3V3 trunk 0.5 mm from C7/C8 to U1 pin 2, E22 pin 9, U3, U4, J4 pin 4, display. VSYS 0.6 mm to J7. VBAT 0.4 mm to U7, U8, J1 pin 20, U11.\n7  GND: one via right beside every GND pad down to In1 (0.6/0.3). Thermal pads (U10, U12, U8, U4) get 3-5 vias. No GND traces.\n8  Signals: I2C (U4, U6, U7, U11, U5, J5, J7), SPI (U2, J4), UARTs (U3, J6), keys (D-pad -> U4), LED1 (U4), SIREN, HAPTIC. 0.15-0.2 mm, F.Cu/B.Cu,\n   cross on In2 only where you must. Decoupling caps: pad -> via, shortest path to the IC pin.\n9  Keep-outs: ESP32 antenna (right of U1, all layers), GNSS antenna, under E22 on B.Cu, SMA launch. DRC enforces them.\n10 Finish: GND stitching vias around the edge every ~5 mm, refill zones, DRC = 0 errors and 0 unconnected, then check RF/USB in 3D view and Gerbers.\nKeys: X route, 6 diff pair, V via, / posture, L lock finished tracks. Set the router to Walk Around so it never shoves RF lines."
		(at 167 123 0)
		(layer "Cmts.User")
		(uuid "3043d244-4689-4bb2-b034-ed1303f3fd73")
